{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795700026,"nonce":"IlC/Qb6fEAmKDTjiFkrHGg0R/Sw=","title":"Two tests in test_fem_march_stats.py fail on main: the deferred solve line and the solve docstring","message":"Two tests in tests/test_fem_march_stats.py fail on main on CPU (`JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu`). Both look like tests that did not follow a library change.\n\n**1. test_the_post_solve_line_does_no_matvec.** The test calls `fem.solve()` and then `fem._solved_line(out, 0.1)`, expecting the range `\"u in [0, \"` in the line. `fem.solve()` now returns a deferred trace node, so the line is\n`solved: linear · deferred (trace node) — built in 0.1 s, the solve runs when you evaluate it through jno.core`\nwith no value range. The property the test protects (the post-solve line costs no matvec) is then not tested at all, because the line never reaches the code that computes the range.\n\n**2. test_the_logging_wrapper_keeps_the_solve_signature_and_docs.** It asserts `FEM.solve.__doc__ == FEM._solve_inner.__doc__`. The wrapper's docstring (copied from `_solve_inner` by the docstring-from marker in jno/_fem.py) has an extra paragraph that `_solve_inner`'s lacks: \"``log=True`` prints each Newton step and each time step while the solve runs (``log=N``: every N-th step of each loop, and its last), ... A deferred solve reports when it is evaluated. Off by default, ...\". The signature assertions before it pass.\n\n**Reproduce.**\n`JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu pytest tests/test_fem_march_stats.py::test_the_post_solve_line_does_no_matvec tests/test_fem_march_stats.py::test_the_logging_wrapper_keeps_the_solve_signature_and_docs`\n\n**Expected.** Tests that pass on main, or fail on a real regression. (1) must evaluate the deferred solve (through jno.core, as the line says) so the line it checks is the evaluated one. (2) must compare the two docstrings under the rule the code actually has: the wrapper's `log=` paragraph is documentation of the wrapper and belongs in `_solve_inner`'s docstring too, or the test should compare after removing that paragraph.\n\n**Where.** tests/test_fem_march_stats.py (both tests); jno/_fem.py `FEM.solve` wrapper and `_solve_inner` docstrings.\n\n**Workaround.** None needed at run time; this only affects the test run.\n\n**Direction.** Update test (1) to force evaluation before calling `_solved_line`; make the `log=` paragraph live in one place so both docstrings agree, which is what test (2) guards.","files":null}]}